# ── IDE-run env overrides (host side) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and adjust. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# NOTE on supported paths: the supported local dev path for this project is
# `docker compose up` (container-first — matches the production target in
# MISSION.md and the AWS-deployable stance). Running patient-service from the
# IDE is an ESCAPE HATCH for debugging / fast inner-loop iteration, not the
# primary path. This file exists so the escape hatch works when you reach for
# it; it is not maintained as a first-class environment going forward.
#
# What this is for:
#   When you launch patient-service from VS Code (Launch config
#   "Spring Boot-PatientServiceApplication<patient-service>"), the app runs on
#   your HOST, not inside the docker network. The broker's in-network hostname
#   `kafka` does not resolve on the host, so you must point at the broker's
#   EXTERNAL listener (`localhost:9094`) instead.
#
# How it gets loaded:
#   `.vscode/launch.json` has, on the patient-service config:
#       "envFile": ["${workspaceFolder}/.env", "${workspaceFolder}/.env.local"]
#   VS Code's Java extension reads both files as `KEY=VALUE` lines and injects
#   them as environment variables at launch. Files are applied left-to-right,
#   so `.env.local` (loaded second) OVERRIDES `.env` (loaded first). That is
#   exactly how a host-side value knocks out the container-side value here.
#
#   - `KEY=VALUE` syntax only. Comments (`#`) and blank lines are fine.
#   - No shell interpolation (`${OTHER}`), no quotes around values.
#   - Only affects the VS Code run config that lists `envFile`. The
#     `BillingServiceApplication` config has no `envFile`, so it's unaffected.
#
# docker-compose runs do NOT read `.env.local`; they read `.env` and use the
# `kafka:9092` in-network address. So the two files cleanly serve the two
# contexts without ever fighting.

# ── Kafka (IDE / host path; docker-compose uses .env's kafka:9092 instead) ───
SPRING_KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=localhost:9094
